  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Calm native operation",
    "overview": "This record applies only to Updates and its integration with Terminal & Linux Settings. It extends Pandora's existing Material 3 interface and restrained purple identity. It does not establish a replacement app-wide system. The direction is Operate: help a user check installed tools, review consequences, run maintenance, and understand the result.\n\nImplementation is the authority: [RuntimeUpdatesScreen.kt](../../app/src/main/java/com/pandora/mobile/RuntimeUpdatesScreen.kt), [SettingsArchitecture.kt](../../app/src/main/java/com/pandora/mobile/SettingsArchitecture.kt), [ImpactPreflight.kt](../../app/src/main/java/com/pandora/mobile/ImpactPreflight.kt), and [PandoraTheme.kt](../../app/src/main/java/com/pandora/mobile/PandoraTheme.kt). The frontmatter records observed light-theme roles and repeated native spacing in dp. Theme selection and remaining Material defaults stay in code. The sidecar contains illustrative browser translations for documentation; its CSS, interaction states, and synthesized tonal ramps are not Android implementation tokens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Plain rows with installed and available versions.",
      "A readable operation summary with optional technical detail.",
      "Explicit session-stop confirmation and bounded recovery."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State in Words Rule",
        "body": "Version, readiness, progress, and error meaning remain explicit in text; color supplements them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Summary First Rule",
        "body": "Keep operation meaning in the normal body role; reserve smaller text and disclosures for technical output.",
        "section": "typography"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the existing Material theme and semantic type roles.",
      "**Do** keep operation summaries visible when diagnostics are collapsed.",
      "**Do** state session interruption and recovery limits before confirmation.",
      "**Do** distinguish actual operation evidence from saved-status UI fixtures."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** turn this Settings extension into a new app-wide visual identity.",
      "**Don't** imply executable rollback restores Debian packages or Codex data.",
      "**Don't** replace operation meaning with raw command output.",
      "**Don't** treat illustrative browser previews as native accessibility or rendering verification."
    ]
  }
